From 17e554a0999e25c5f6d68c6caf8446755bbf930d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 11:49:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 287: the negative control was ill-posed - and the span
 channel is 1.3% of a layer

The control fired and it was right to fire: MEASUREMENT_BROKEN on both spans,
null AUC 0.163 at -12 sigma where 0.5 was required. But the fault is mine and
it is in the control, not in the estimator.

Regressing a channel on ITSELF cannot read chance. lstsq returns a slope of
1 - eps, so the residual is eps*L - delta: a perfectly monotone function of L
at machine scale, whose AUC is therefore AUC(L) or 1 - AUC(L) and never 0.5.
Reproduced exactly - with eps positive the null reads 0.989, with eps negative
0.011, and the run's 0.163 is that same mechanism with partial cancellation.
The control was ill-posed by construction, which is a fourth species of the
vacuous-gate family and now recorded as such.

Two well-posed nulls replace it. A LABEL PERMUTATION null keeps the real
residual and shuffles which pairs are same-address, 99 times; it tests the
whole path including the fit and is the standard null for this statistic. A
REDUNDANT-CHANNEL null builds an affine copy of the lower cosine plus noise at
the observed residual scale - a channel with real residual variance and no
unique class content. Verified offline: permutation reads 0.503-0.506 at
|z| < 0.2 in every case, a redundant-plus-noise channel reads 0.487, and a
channel carrying planted unique signal is still detected at 0.703, z = +7.2.
The gate rides on the permutation null alone, because the redundant one
degenerates whenever the real residual is dust - it would then reproduce the
failure it replaced - so it is reported as a diagnostic instead.

What the run already says, and the fix does not change, because these numbers
never depended on the broken control:

  The lower ink is order-blind to 4.5e-08, which is float32 noise. The wiring
  proof passes and the double order-blindness is now measured rather than
  argued from the source.

  The upper ink DOES see word order, and the amount is the finding: median
  cos(U, U_shuffled) = 0.987 at span 2 and 0.987 at span 3. Destroying word
  order entirely moves the vector by 1.3%. Spearman against the lower channel
  is 0.959. It is not a second layer, it is the first layer with a 1.3%
  perturbation - which is why the residual carries no unique signal (AUC 0.494
  and 0.467, both at or below chance on a residual whose magnitude is far
  above dust, so those two numbers are trustworthy as they stand).

The mechanism is now clear enough to state: fp(span) has the sum of its
members' character histograms, and averaging over overlapping spans nearly
commutes back to averaging over words, because the feed-forward is close to
linear across the region these histograms occupy. The nonlinearity argument
was correct in principle and 1.3% in magnitude.

order_content = 1 - median cos is now a reported headline, so the next
candidate upper layer is judged by how much of it it actually has before
anything else is measured about it.

