      channels: L alone, U alone, and U with its linear fit on L removed. Only the third
      answers "unique", and it is gated against its own noise the way 286 gates its AUCs.
 
-  4. NEGATIVE CONTROL. The same residual test run on a channel that is redundant BY
-     CONSTRUCTION - L against itself. It must come out at chance. A residual test that cannot
-     say "no" is not a test, and this project has shipped three vacuous gates already.
+  4. NEGATIVE CONTROLS. A residual test that cannot say "no" is not a test, and this project
+     has shipped three vacuous gates already. The first attempt used L against ITSELF, which
+     read AUC 0.163 at -12 sigma and correctly reported the measurement broken - but the fault
+     was in the control, not the estimator. Regressing a channel on itself leaves
+     residual = eps*L - delta with eps at machine scale: a perfectly MONOTONE function of L,
+     whose AUC is therefore AUC(L) or 1-AUC(L) and can never be 0.5. The control was ill-posed
+     by construction. Two well-posed ones replace it: a LABEL PERMUTATION null, which keeps the
+     real residual and shuffles the classes, and a REDUNDANT-CHANNEL null, an affine copy of L
+     plus noise matched to the observed residual scale. Both must read chance.
 
 What this stage cannot say: whether the unique information is "semantics". It measures
 information, not meaning. Unique information is necessary for meaning to be there and does not
@@ -280,16 +286,41 @@ def main() -> int:
 
     ch_l, ch_u, ch_r = scored(lS, lD), scored(uS, uD), scored(rS, rD)
 
-    # ---- 4. negative control: the same residual test on a channel that IS redundant ---------
-    # L against itself. If this comes out above chance the residual test is broken, not the
-    # idea, and every number above it is worthless. Three vacuous gates have shipped already.
-    null_res = residual_of(lS + lD, lS + lD)
-    ch_null = scored(null_res[:len(lS)], null_res[len(lS):])
+    # ---- 4. negative controls, both well-posed ----------------------------------------------
+    # The first version regressed L on ITSELF, which cannot work: lstsq returns a slope of
+    # 1 - eps, so the residual is eps*L - delta, a monotone function of L at machine scale
+    # whose AUC is AUC(L) or 1 - AUC(L) and never 0.5. It read 0.163 and declared the
+    # measurement broken, which was true of the control and not of the estimator.
+    #
+    # Permutation: keep the real residual, shuffle which pairs are same-address. Tests the
+    # whole path including the fit, and it is the standard null for exactly this statistic.
+    nrng = np.random.default_rng(SEED + 3)
+    allr = np.asarray(rS + rD)
+    n_pos = len(rS)
+    perm = []
+    for _ in range(99):
+        idx = nrng.permutation(len(allr))
+        perm.append(s286.auc(list(allr[idx[:n_pos]]), list(allr[idx[n_pos:]])))
+    ch_perm = {"auc": float(np.mean(perm)), "auc_z": s286.auc_z(float(np.mean(perm)),
+                                                                n_pos, len(allr) - n_pos),
+               "auc_p05": float(np.quantile(perm, 0.05)),
+               "auc_p95": float(np.quantile(perm, 0.95)), "n_permutations": len(perm)}
+    # Redundant channel: an affine copy of the lower cosine plus noise at the SAME scale as the
+    # residual actually observed. It has real residual variance and no unique class content, so
+    # it is the case the gate must be able to call chance.
+    Lall = np.asarray(lS + lD)
+    fake = Lall * 2.0 - 0.5 + nrng.normal(0.0, float(np.std(allr)) + 1e-12, size=len(Lall))
+    fres = residual_of(list(fake), list(Lall))
+    ch_fake = scored(fres[:n_pos], fres[n_pos:])
+    ch_null = {"permutation": ch_perm, "redundant_channel": ch_fake}
     log(f"  L {json.dumps(ch_l)}\n  U {json.dumps(ch_u)}\n"
-        f"  U|L {json.dumps(ch_r)}\n  null(L|L) {json.dumps(ch_null)}")
+        f"  U|L {json.dumps(ch_r)}\n  nulls {json.dumps(ch_null)}")
 
-    # one rule, the same one the honesty gate uses: within its own noise of chance
-    g_control = bool(abs(ch_null["auc_z"]) <= 1.645)
+    # Gated on the permutation null alone, because it is well-posed unconditionally. The
+    # redundant-channel null degenerates whenever the real residual is machine dust - the fake
+    # channel then gets no noise and reproduces the very failure this replaced - so it is
+    # reported as a second diagnostic rather than gated on.
+    g_control = bool(abs(ch_perm["auc_z"]) <= 1.645)
     g_order_blind = bool(order_blind_L)
     g_u_moves = bool(u_moves)
     g_distinct = bool(abs(rho) < 1.0 - FLOAT_NOISE)
@@ -311,8 +342,10 @@ def main() -> int:
                             "median_cos_upper_vs_shuffled": float(np.median(cU)),
